  "question": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>-digit numbers are formed using only three digits <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>. The smallest value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;for which&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>900</mn></math> such distinct numbers can be formed is :"
