  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>- digit number are formed using only three digits&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>&nbsp;with repetition&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></math>.</p><p>Since,&nbsp;<math><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>900</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>900</mn></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math>.</p>"
